# Kept in the repository, never deployed.
#
# docs/ holds working notes and the EV for Artists programme drafts, including
# the private Collaboration Agreement. That one must not be reachable at a
# public URL — it is a contract template under review, not a published policy.
# The two documents an artist actually has to read before submitting
# (Submission Terms, Submission Privacy Notice) are real pages under /legal
# and ARE deployed.
docs/

# Database migrations. Applied with the Supabase CLI, never served.
supabase/

# Source renders and project files for motion work. Large, and nothing serves
# them.
assets/After Effects Assets/
enter-the-void.mov

# mobile-app/ and void-native/ are deliberately left in: mobile-app deploys
# from its own Vercel project rooted at that directory, and an ignore rule
# here is not worth the risk of reaching it.

# Executable tests. They apply the migrations and import the API handlers, so
# they belong in the repository — but nothing serves them.
tests/
